    "Description": "P2 proof (Hill-attack -> Blueprints migration): a from-scratch, blueprint-authored AiPrimitive BTreeCondition proving the NEW visually-native GetComponent node end-to-end -- an ECS component field read with NO CLR reflection at generation time. Graph: EventEntry -> Branch, fed by GetComponent(self, Fdp.Toolkit.Navigation.NavigationStatus.Result) [no 'Target' pin wired -- self-default, emits IrOp_Self] -> FunctionCall HillAssault2NavOps.IsArrived(result) [IsPure, TrailingContext: None -- a contextless helper, proving the baked-context path also handles the 'no self/view' case] -> Branch.Condition -> Return(Success)/Return(Failure). GAP-12: blueprints have no native comparison/equality node yet, so the enum-equality check (NavigationResult == NavigationResult.Arrived) that turns the GetComponent field read into a bool condition lives in the tiny pure HillAssault2NavOps.IsArrived helper (Hrot.AI.Behaviors/Brains/HillAssault2NavOps.cs) -- a stopgap deleted once a native Compare node lands, at which point this condition becomes fully visual. Does not modify the C# oracle. See HillAssault2_IsSelfArrived_ProofTests.cs, which reflects the real generated Hrot.AI.Behaviors.Generated.HillAssault2IsSelfArrived_*_Bp type out of the built Hrot.AI.Behaviors.dll and asserts the generated TickCore body contains 'GetComponentRO<global::Fdp.Toolkit.Navigation.NavigationStatus>', '.Result', and 'HillAssault2NavOps.IsArrived('.",
